  "notes": [
    "Values digitised from Schmid 2020 (mean and range of Polga 2004); means checked against Dreischarf 2016.",
    "Meir 2007 is excluded: intraoperative profilometry in anaesthetised, side-lying patients, no loaded task.",
    "Thoracic discs show ~0.2-0.3 MPa even unloaded; Eq. 6 is a lumbar relation applied unchanged."
  ],
  "agent_prompt": "Use your spine musculoskeletal model. Scale it to the Polga 2004 subject in \"subjects\" (male, 33 y, 178 cm, 73 kg). For each task in \"tasks\", simulate the posture and hand load given in its inputs. Compute compression and flexion at T6-T7 and T7-T8 (average them for \"mid\") and at T9-T10 and T10-T11 (average for \"lower\"), and convert to intradiscal pressure with Ghezelbash 2016 Eq. 6 (P = F/A, A = 663 mm2 mid, 897 mm2 lower) or IDP = F/(0.66 A); say which. Do not tune the model to the reference values. Return JSON shaped like \"answer_format\": one entry per task id with IDP in MPa.",
